From 18433a93512cf5b3534862b828f9225620ac13f1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 18:27:08 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat: wire homepage About/Gallery/Radio/CTA sections to
 Sanity CMS
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Closes the 4 gaps found in the CMS coverage audit:

- AboutPreview now reads aboutPage.whoWeAre (title/p1/p2) via
  useAboutPage() — that content already exists in Sanity from the
  About page work, so no migration is needed here.
- GalleryPreview now reads the existing galleryEvent collection via
  useGalleryEvents(), flattening the first 5 photos across
  collections (ordered); falls back to the hardcoded album once
  there are 5+ real photos to fill the fixed 4x2 grid.
- RadioSection (homepage teaser) and CTABanner now read from
  siteSettings: radio.desc/pillars (new fields) plus the existing
  radio.tagline/frequency/listenUrl, and a new cta.title/desc object.
- Also fixed useSiteSettings() to properly resolve radio.tagline as
  a localized field (it was passed through unresolved before) and
  added desc/pillars/cta resolution alongside it.
- CTABanner was fully built but never mounted anywhere — added it to
  Home.tsx as the closing section before the footer.

Includes scripts/migrate-homepage-teasers.mjs (dry-run by default)
to seed the two genuinely new siteSettings fields (radio.desc,
radio.pillars, cta.title, cta.desc) from the current hardcoded
home.json copy, additive-only and safe to re-run.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_012xNEugH42JGJDBqiHFtfyU
